you're looking at Miami Florida home of  the Miami Dolphins and the site of next  year's Super Bowl now only on CBS this  morning we are seeing firsthand how  staff at major sports arenas are  learning how to save lives  Jamie wax went behind the scenes at Hard  Rock Stadium to find out how employees  are being trained to use trauma kits  after a major accident or attack this is  our trauma bandage all right it's pretty  straightforward this may be the locker  room with the Miami Dolphins  but these drills we're at about 20  seconds have nothing to do with football  21:22 for two days we watched as Stadium  employees from interns to the CEO  learned how to stop traumatic bleeding  and injury if you can put it on your leg  you can put it on somebody else their  coach was Lieutenant Dan stout a 25 year  law enforcement veteran who now works  for tactical medical solutions pack pack  pack pack pack the Dolphins hired the  company to install multiple public  access trauma kits throughout Hard Rock  Stadium and trained its workers on how  to use them it's far more than a  first-aid kit right that's correct these  are stocked with the same equipment that  we give to our military the same  equipment that we give to our first  responders this kit is for very serious  critical stuff whether it's an attack on  an arena in England  or a high school just half an hour from  here  stout told us first responders arrived  at the scene and find civilians coming  to the aid of their neighbors they're  trying to improvise bandages with shirts  they're trying to make tourniquets out  of belts they know what they need what  we're trying to do is provide them with  a basis of training and access to the  right equipment in places where they may  encounter this type of thing how much  difference can it make as far as  survival to have these items close by a  lot of these injuries you've got four to  six minutes to make a difference on  whether that person lives or dies the  kids are packed with step-by-step  instructions and color-coded packaging  which appealed to Dave lassen director  of stadium security do you feel like  your people are safer because of it  absolutely I think anybody can pick this  up and assist which is the end goal is  just to get somebody to a higher echelon  medical care Sidney Williams an event  coordinator with the team says she is  grateful for the extra training  you always know like something like this  could happen really for me I feel a lot  more comfortable knowing that we do have  the appropriate procedures in place so  it makes you feel more safe yes other  stadiums have added similar kits  Gillette Stadium home of the New England  Patriots was the first NFL venue to  install them the New Orleans Saints and  Major League Baseball's New York Yankees  followed for Tom Garfinkel the CEO of  the Miami Dolphins it was an easy  decision we just want to make sure we're  doing everything we can here to make  this the safest environment possible for  our employees and for all of our guests  and everybody that comes and as you say  you take that very personally I do I  want to be able to sleep at night I want  to know that everybody here is safe and  that we've done everything we can to  prevent it from happening and if it does  happen make sure we're responding and  doing everything we can to save lives  the Dolphins organization including  owner Stephen Ross stressed that this  kind of preparedness is important to any  office environment whether the potential  injuries are due to traumatic events or  simply workplace accidents I have to say  watching the training there was a  generational divide the  older folks they're sort of had a  dramatic reaction to what we were doing  and what that represented and the  younger generation was very pragmatic  about it yes though this is just  something that happens in our world the  older generation was dramatic how what  do you mean I mean it's it's emotional  to watch all of these people yeah  wounds and imagine what what that would  look like in real life and the younger  people saying this is a sign of the time  I don't remember this one I was going to  the kids have grown up with it and the  grown-ups really didn't yeah it sure  makes a lot of sense it does I mean if  you if you can't prevent these things  from happening at least you can save  lives and everyone said even if this  represents the worst-case scenario if  you can save one life with these kids I  would only point out that there are a  lot of people out there who say you can  prevent this kind of thing exactly there  are steps to take you got to be ready
 

